ComfyUI-BCNodes — models/qwen_image/dype/

This directory contains code derived from ComfyUI-DyPE
(https://github.com/wildminder/ComfyUI-DyPE), by wildminder and the ComfyUI-DyPE contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory). The sources are the
files src/models/qwen.py (PosEmbedQwen) and src/base.py (the branches of DyPEBasePosEmbed it runs:
_calc_vision_yarn_components, _calc_yarn_components with and without yarn_alt_scaling, _get_mscale)
at commit 266405844738da9f16e8a072482320168a17c494 (2026-10-24, version 2.20.0).

ComfyUI-DyPE implements DyPE, Dynamic Position Extrapolation, by Noam Issachar, Guy Yariv and
co-authors (https://github.com/guyyariv/DyPE).

Changes made in ComfyUI-BCNodes (embedder.py):
- The scale of each image axis is the latent's side in pixels over base_resolution, read from the
  latent of each call (an area crop's own). The original read it from the span of every position id given to
  the embedder. On ComfyUI core's Qwen-Image those ids hold the caption tokens too, placed after the
  image's positions on all three axes, so the original's scale grew with the prompt's length (at
  1328 x 1328 px with 100 caption tokens it extrapolated at 2.19x the base resolution); and its span
  cache was keyed by the tensor's shape only, so the columns took the rows' span (a landscape image
  was scaled by its height).
- Every frequency table is computed in float64 on a device that supports it (the CPU otherwise)
  and the rotations are returned in float32, as ComfyUI core's rope; the original computed them in
  bfloat16 on CUDA and float32 elsewhere.
- yarn (without yarn_alt_scaling) takes its table at the positions core gives. The original looked
  the table up from 0 at the lowest position, clamped to the table's length: the same rotation
  between any two tokens of an axis, RoPE being relative, without the clamp.
- The rotation layout, the time axis and the ntk, pi and base tables are the ones every model shares
  (libs/dype/embed.py).
- The shift override of the original installer (src/patch_utils.py, a model_sampling replaced by a
  resolution-dependent ModelSamplingFlux) is not ported: the model's own shift is kept.
- The embedder is built for one call size of a sampling step, with that scale, the step's
  timestep and the settings fixed, and set on the model (and on an InstantX ControlNet's model) only
  for the duration of the step (models/common/dype.py); the original set state on one embedder
  installed as an object patch.
